<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pravarapura</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pravarapura was a capital of the main branch of the Vakataka dynasty in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pravarasena-ii">Pravarasena II</a> in the 5th century. It is identified with Pavnar near Wardha in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, where excavations and sculptures of the Vakataka period, including scenes from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a>, have been found. Several of Pravarasena II's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants were issued from it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pravarapura.jpg" alt="Pravarapura" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Syed barid · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hazrath_Fariduddin_Ganj_Shakkar_Chilla_Place.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
